  "summary": "Postinstall beacon exfiltrates host and CI identifiers to hardcoded bare-IP endpoint",
  "details": "On npm install, the package's postinstall script runs `node./index.cjs`, which collects installer host identifiers (hostname, home directory path, platform) and detects the CI provider by reading multiple environment variables, then POSTs the result as JSON to a hardcoded bare-IP HTTPS endpoint at https://130.162.231.177:8443/. The destination is a bare IPv4 address on an unusual port, not tied to any declared publisher domain, with no documentation or opt-in. This is an install-time reconnaissance beacon against the installer.",
